# 15-to-1 magic-state distillation (Bravyi & Kitaev 2005), on the [[15,1,3]] quantum
# Reed-Muller code: the factory's protocol, one operation a line.  The msf15 place compiles
# exactly this (qccd/gadget/leaves/factory.py, ring_circuit), every TSIR gate, reset and
# measurement naming the line it realises; its logic check runs it as a state vector.
#
# qubits 0..14 are the code's 15 positions (column j of the code holds the binary digits
# of j+1).  The |+> of the code is the uniform superposition over the classical [15,5] code
# spanned by the all-ones word and the four bit rows; in row echelon form its pivots are
# {0, 1, 2, 3, 7}.  Transversal T on the code is logical T-dagger.  All 14 outcomes 0 is the
# post-selection; qubit 0 then holds T-dagger|+>.

output 0

# every ion fresh
reset 0
reset 1
reset 2
reset 3
reset 4
reset 5
reset 6
reset 7
reset 8
reset 9
reset 10
reset 11
reset 12
reset 13
reset 14

# the encoder: the pivots in |+>, fanned out over the code's rows
H 0
H 1
H 2
H 3
H 7
CX 0 5
CX 0 6
CX 0 9
CX 0 10
CX 0 11
CX 0 12
CX 1 4
CX 1 6
CX 1 8
CX 1 10
CX 1 11
CX 1 13
CX 2 4
CX 2 5
CX 2 8
CX 2 9
CX 2 11
CX 2 14
CX 3 4
CX 3 5
CX 3 6
CX 3 11
CX 3 12
CX 3 13
CX 3 14
CX 7 8
CX 7 9
CX 7 10
CX 7 11
CX 7 12
CX 7 13
CX 7 14

# transversal T: logical T-dagger on the code
T 0
T 1
T 2
T 3
T 4
T 5
T 6
T 7
T 8
T 9
T 10
T 11
T 12
T 13
T 14

# the encoder again, which is its own inverse (its CNOTs commute)
CX 0 5
CX 0 6
CX 0 9
CX 0 10
CX 0 11
CX 0 12
CX 1 4
CX 1 6
CX 1 8
CX 1 10
CX 1 11
CX 1 13
CX 2 4
CX 2 5
CX 2 8
CX 2 9
CX 2 11
CX 2 14
CX 3 4
CX 3 5
CX 3 6
CX 3 11
CX 3 12
CX 3 13
CX 3 14
CX 7 8
CX 7 9
CX 7 10
CX 7 11
CX 7 12
CX 7 13
CX 7 14

# fold the phase onto the output: it sits on the parity of the first three pivots
CX 1 0
CX 2 0

# read the syndromes: the other pivots in X, the non-pivots in Z
H 1
H 2
H 3
H 7
measure 1
measure 2
measure 3
measure 4
measure 5
measure 6
measure 7
measure 8
measure 9
measure 10
measure 11
measure 12
measure 13
measure 14
